+//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
+//
+// Post-RA formation of `ldm.o` / `stm.o` (LLVM-129t).
+//
+// The ISA addresses a multi-register transfer with
+//   ldm.o {rdHA : rdHA+immu6-1}, [rbHB, rdHC]
+//   stm.o  rdHA, rbHB, rdHC, immu6
+// i.e. register `rdHA+i` is loaded from / stored to `rbHB + rdHC + 8*i`
+// (spec/SimRISC-01 §存取RD寄存器, §存取RB寄存器).  The register range is a
+// *contiguous* run of the same bank and `immu6` counts it (`start + immu6 <=
+// 64`, `immu6 != 0`; contracts/legality_rules.yaml::mreg_zero / mreg_range_*).
+//
+// Why post-RA: the addresses and — decisively — the *physical* register numbers
+// only exist after register allocation.  Whether two adjacent accesses land in
+// consecutive registers is decided by the allocator, so a pre-RA transformation
+// can at best raise the probability (ARM's ARMLoadStoreOptimizer does its
+// address-sorting pre-RA and the real merging post-RA for exactly this reason).
+// This pass therefore runs in addPreEmitPass, after PEI has eliminated frame
+// indices and inserted the prologue/epilogue, so every access is a concrete
+// `[base, imm]` and the merged instruction can be emitted directly.
+//
+// Merging rules (all must hold; anything else is left untouched):
+//   * same basic block, *strictly adjacent* memory instructions (only debug
+//     instructions may sit between them).  This is what makes the pass safe
+//     against reordering: no other access, call or barrier can end up between
+//     the merged elements, so no intra-run aliasing is possible.
+//   * same direction (all loads or all stores), same bank (RD or RB — the two
+//     banks are separate register files and must never be mixed), same base
+//     register, and immediate offsets ascending by exactly 8 per element.
+//   * physical registers ascending by exactly 1 per element.
+//   * count >= 2.  A non-zero first offset needs an extra base recomputation
+//     (`rb2rb` + `add.si`, 2 instructions), so it is only profitable at
+//     count >= 4; that path additionally needs a caller-saved RB register that
+//     the whole function never uses (see findScratchRB).
+//   * no volatile/atomic access, and no instruction carrying a
+//     FrameSetup/FrameDestroy flag (prologue/epilogue emission is the frame
+//     lowering's business).
+//
+// Deliberately NOT covered: `memset` (one value replicated into N registers has
+// no multi-register transfer to exploit) and the memory intrinsics' inline
+// expansion beyond the above pattern (their load/store pairs alternate, so the
+// run never reaches count 2 with consecutive destination registers).
+//
+//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
+
+#include "DADAO.h"
+#include "DADAOInstrInfo.h"
+#include "DADAORegisterInfo.h"
+#include "DADAOSubtarget.h"
